@inject ApiMetadata Api
@* Tabs' Overview, written by hand after Button's: picking a tab previewed in each mode, the looks,
   vertical tabs, the tab in the address, tabs in a form and panel padding.
   Parts, Accessibility and See also come from the doc comments and components.json. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>Tabs are a row of labels over panels of content, such as a record's details and its history; the user picks a tab to show its panel. They switch <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">with JavaScript off</Anchor> too. For sections the user opens one by one, see <Anchor Href="docs/components/accordion">Accordion</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Picking a tab</Heading>
<TextBlock>The selected tab is the one whose panel shows. To set the tab that opens first, set <Code>Selected</Code>. On interactive pages, to follow the selected tab from C#, bind it with <Code>@@bind-Selected</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tabs-modes" />
<TextBlock>A tab's value is its <Code>Value</Code>, or its label in lower case with dashes, such as <Code>billing-history</Code>.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>Every panel renders with the page, and picking a tab only shows another panel. Switching is instant, and it keeps what the user typed. Content that's slow to build or rarely opened is better on a page of its own, behind a <Anchor Href="docs/components/tab-nav">TabNav</Anchor> link.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Variants, icons and badges</Heading>
<TextBlock>Tabs come in three variants: an underline (the default), soft tabs, or a segmented control. Set <Code>Variant</Code>. Each <Code>Tab</Code> can have an <Code>Icon</Code> and a <Code>Badge</Code>, or be <Code>Disabled</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tabs-variants" />

<Heading Level="2">Sizes and full width</Heading>
<TextBlock>Tabs can match the size of the controls around them, and they can fill the row. To match the buttons and fields around the tabs, set <Code>Size</Code>. To share the row equally between the tabs, set <Code>FullWidth</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tabs-sizes" />

<Heading Level="2">Vertical</Heading>
<TextBlock>Vertical tabs sit in a column beside the panels, from 640px up. Set <Code>Orientation="Orientation.Vertical"</Code>. On phones, the tabs stay a row above the panels, which scrolls when it doesn't fit.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tabs-vertical" />

<Heading Level="2">In the URL</Heading>
<TextBlock>Tabs can keep the selected tab in the URL, so a link to <Code>?tab=billing</Code> opens Billing, and a copied URL keeps the tab. Set <Code>QueryKey</Code>. The URL overrides <Code>Selected</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tabs-url" />

<Heading Level="2">Closing and adding tabs</Heading>
<TextBlock>Closable tabs suit documents the user opens and closes, such as invoices in an editor. Handle <Code>OnClose</Code> to put a close button on each tab, and remove the tab from your list there. Handle <Code>OnAdd</Code> to show an add button after the tabs.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tabs-closable" />
<List Gap="2">
    <ListItem>The tab stays until it leaves the list. To ask first, as here for an unsaved draft, await a confirmation and remove it only on yes.</ListItem>
    <ListItem><Code>Closable="false"</Code> keeps one tab without a close button.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>When the selected tab closes, the tab after it opens, or the one before when it was last.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>Delete or Backspace on a tab closes it, with script.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>When the tabs don't fit, they scroll and the add button stays at the end of the row.</ListItem>
</List>
<TextBlock>On static pages, closing and adding are links. Set each <Code>Tab</Code>'s <Code>CloseHref</Code> and the tabs' <Code>AddHref</Code> to addresses that drop or add the tab, here by keeping the open invoices in the URL. With <Code>QueryKey</Code> set, a close link carries the tab that's open when it's followed.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tabs-closable-links" />

<Heading Level="2">In a form</Heading>
<TextBlock>Tabs can split a long form. Put <Code>Tabs</Code> inside a <Anchor Href="docs/components/form">Form</Anchor>: every panel is part of the form, so every field posts.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tabs-account-form" />
<TextBlock>When the server finds errors, the first tab with errors opens, unless the open tab has some. Each tab shows how many errors it has. This example sets <Code>NativeValidation="false"</Code> so the server's errors show.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>With the browser's own checks on, the default, the form post waits until they pass. IzzyBlazor's script opens the tab of the first field the browser stops at, so its message shows.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Panel padding</Heading>
<TextBlock>A panel's padding is the space around its content. To pad every panel on all sides, set <Code>ContentPadding</Code>. To run a table edge to edge in one panel, set that <Code>Tab</Code>'s own <Code>ContentPadding="0"</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tabs-padding" />

@if (OverviewParts.Of(Component, Api).Count > 0)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Parts</Heading>
}
<OverviewParts Component="Component" />

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <Tabs Label="Account">
            <Tab Label="Profile" Icon="Lucide.User">...</Tab>
            <Tab Label="Billing" Badge="2">...</Tab>
        </Tabs>
        """;
}
